<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Otrar</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Farab</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Otrar was a medieval oasis city on the middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syr-darya">Syr Darya</a> in southern Kazakhstan, an important town of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk-road">Silk Road</a>. In 1218 its governor massacred a caravan of merchants sent by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genghis-khan">Genghis Khan</a>, the incident that provoked the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-invasion-of-the-khwarazmian-empire">Mongol invasion of the Khwarazmian Empire</a>; the city fell after a long siege. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a> died there in February 1405 as he marched to invade <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. Its ruins are now an archaeological site.</p></div>
